ld: SH: fix relaxation bugs, relax calls across sections

1. sh_elf_relax_delete_bytes: when "mov.l .Lfn,rN; jsr @rN" became
   "bsr fn" for a static fn of the same section, the R_SH_IND12W reloc
   is against the section symbol with the offset in the addend, which
   later deletions did not adjust: the bsr landed inside fn.
   Reproducer: zlib trees.c at -O2 -mrelax ("bsr compress_block+8").

2. sh_elf_relax_delete_bytes: the base of a braf table, the address
   after the braf delay slot, can sit where the deletion stops at an
   alignment (GCC emits "braf; nop; .L1: .align 2; <constant pool>").
   It was treated as a label after the padding that does not move, so
   all entries were off by 2.  Reproducer: gcc.c-torture/execute/
   pr91632.c at -O2 -mrelax.

3. sh_elf_swap_insns: when swapping the register load that an R_SH_USES
   reloc refers to, the code moved r_offset (the jsr) instead of
   r_addend (the load), a leftover of coff-sh.c where the addend field
   is named r_offset.  The jsr->bsr rewrite then hit the delay slot.
   Reproducer: gcc.c-torture/execute/pr53645-2.c at -Os -mrelax.

4. sh_elf_relax_section: a call to a static function in another
   section of the same object (every call, with -ffunction-sections)
   was not relaxed and warned "symbol in unexpected section".  Relax
   it, and adjust the R_SH_IND12W addend when the target section
   shrinks.

